              "ImageDescription": {
                "value": "Circular cast, lead alloy, post-medieval weight.  The obverse has a relief border containing a band of lettering in relief reading ELISABE..AN 1634 (the number 4 is reversed) all within two relief lines (one above and one below the lettering).  At the centre, within a further circle in relief, is a stylised Tudor rose.  The reverse has a crude spiral scratched into the surface.<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p>\n<p>The object is circular in shape but has been slightly damaged in the plough soil.  It has a powdery white patina.</p>\n<p>Diameter: 34.3mm; weight: 15.5g</p>",
                "source": "commons-desc-page"
              },
