                "value": "<div class=\"fn value\">\nThe Portable Antiquities Scheme, Susie White, 2016-10-24 09:50:26</div>",
                "source": "commons-desc-page"
              },
              "ImageDescription": {
                "value": "<div>\n<p>A medieval copper-alloy English jetton. Mid-to-late 14th-century lion type depicting a lion rampant within elaborate border, Mernick reference 5a.4 (reverse 22), dating to the later reign of Edward III or Richard II, possibly c. 1350-1380. Mint uncertain.</p>\nThis jetton is not readily apparent in the main literature though this late English lion type has recently been web published by Mernick. However this particular reverse type (22 within the series) was not yet known with this obverse.</div>\n<p><span>Ref: Mernick 5a.4 (reverse 22).</span></p>",
                "source": "commons-desc-page"
              },
              "DateTimeOriginal": {
                "value": "between 1350 and 1380<div style=\"display: none;\">date QS:P571,+1350-00-00T00:00:00Z/7,P1319,+1350-00-00T00:00:00Z/9,P1326,+1380-00-00T00:00:00Z/9</div>",
